# A declined "up to one" target must not skip the spell's later targets
# (CR 601.2c). Reproduction of an open engine bug: a stack object's
# targets are one flat list, so a declined optional target has no place
# in it, and the engine ends targeting there (`Choice::Done`, or no legal
# choice for the optional target) rather than shift the later targets.

scenario "Explosive Entry with no artifact still puts a counter on a creature" {
  skip "engine bug: a declined up-to target skips the later targets"
  battlefield A: 2 "Mountain", "Grizzly Bears"
  hand A: "Explosive Entry"
  turn 1 A: cast "Explosive Entry" targeting "Grizzly Bears"
  run_to turn 1 postcombat_main
  assert counters "Grizzly Bears" +1/+1 1
}
